WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.090
- Is it true that it's
your first talk show?

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:03.461
- Yes, it is my first talk show.

00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:05.558
- First talk show!
(audience applause)

00:00:05.558 --> 00:00:06.391
Yes!

00:00:06.391 --> 00:00:08.340
Okay, I might have made something for you.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.840
I mean, whatever, Alison
made the really good one.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.140
But like, which one would you like?

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.189
Which one would you like?

00:00:15.189 --> 00:00:16.071
(laughter)

00:00:16.071 --> 00:00:17.381
I'm just kidding.

00:00:17.381 --> 00:00:18.510
- I mean.
- Which one?

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.480
- I love pink.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.490
- Okay.
- It's a good color.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.323
- You know what,

00:00:21.323 --> 00:00:22.669
this is a special...
- This one's cute.

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:23.981
- That's the one.
- Something.

00:00:23.981 --> 00:00:25.272
- [Alison] That's the one that you chose.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:27.252
- This will go in my bedroom.

00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:28.467
- Its a really messed up giraffe.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.537
I just started.

00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:30.370
- Great room decor.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.936
- [Kelly] Don't judge me Ella.
- Okay (laughs).

00:00:31.936 --> 00:00:32.769
(laughter)
- I just started.

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:33.602
I thought you were totally gonna

00:00:33.602 --> 00:00:35.058
pick Alison's cause it's legit.

00:00:35.058 --> 00:00:36.278
(laughter)

00:00:36.278 --> 00:00:38.170
- I'm good with this one.
- I like you more for that.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.960
So what was your first talk show Alison?

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.857
- I think it was Craig Ferguson.

00:00:41.857 --> 00:00:43.090
- [Kelly] (gasp) Love Craig Ferguson.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.460
- Yeah it was really fun.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.410
- He's funny.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.680
- He was so funny.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.380
It was a really great time,
but I do remember getting...

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.488
I was very nervous.

00:00:50.488 --> 00:00:52.120
- I'm nervous

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:52.953
- Yes and there's a lot

00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:54.660
of people around you.
- Oh, this is so chill.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.870
- This is very chill,

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.963
but there sometimes can be
people that stress you out.

00:00:59.877 --> 00:01:01.290
(laughter)

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.270
Like, don't you get so stressed
and people stress you out?

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.103
- Oh my God.
- Like you should

00:01:04.103 --> 00:01:07.010
be super stressed.
(laughter)

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.910
I think the best thing
is just to be yourself,

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.100
'cause everyone's trying to remind you

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.700
what to say and what to do and like--

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.623
- [Kelly] Just be you.

00:01:12.623 --> 00:01:13.456
- You gotta just go with the flow.

00:01:13.456 --> 00:01:14.810
- Yeah, and you're cool.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:15.977
Great acting.

00:01:15.977 --> 00:01:16.810
- (laughs) Thank you.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.643
- You're so young.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.528
Like to be doing that's crazy.
(audience applause)

00:01:19.528 --> 00:01:20.361
- Thank you.

00:01:20.361 --> 00:01:21.600
- What is the coolest thing,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.730
about being a part of this movie?

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.170
- I think the coolest thing about

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.558
being part of this movie in particular,

00:01:27.558 --> 00:01:30.539
is that Harley Quinn
doesn't care about anything,

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:33.750
she's just so crazy and it was so fun

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.157
to be with her and to just mess
around and be a kid on set.

00:01:38.157 --> 00:01:39.270
- Yes, that's so fun.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.350
Well it's good when you...

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.980
You'll learn that too, just
working on different sets

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.619
with different actors and
different people like,

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:46.700
especially if you start out so nice

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.850
with somebody that's really cool

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.230
and let's you just be you and
isn't giving added pressure.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.189
Those are the jobs you want.

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:55.740
So your character Birds
of Prey is a pickpocket.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.149
So did you study hard for that one?

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:00.130
(laughter)

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.768
Where's my wallet, is what I'm saying.

00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:02.601
(laughter)

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:03.736
- I would be careful with that one.

00:02:03.736 --> 00:02:04.569
(laughter)

00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:06.730
But, a magician from the Magic Castle,

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:10.030
he came and taught me how to pickpocket

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:14.180
and how to work with a little
bit of magic and cards and--

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.050
- I've always wanted to
go to the Magic Castle,

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.150
like what did the do there?

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.212
It just seems like they pickpocket,

00:02:20.212 --> 00:02:21.130
that's what they do.
- Pickpocket.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.552
- Maybe I don't wanna go
there, I like my money.

00:02:23.552 --> 00:02:26.830
So what is the key to stealing a wallet?

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.231
Just asking for a friend.

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:30.560
(laughter)

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.890
- Well a magician never
gives away their secrets.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.110
- Oh, I like you, I like you.
(laughter)

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.833
Well we have a magician next,

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.070
so if you, if the both of you,

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.500
I always love asking people this,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.621
usually it's after several
drinks, but don't drink.

00:02:42.621 --> 00:02:43.454
- Okay (laughs).

00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:46.190
- So what super power would you want,

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.670
if you could pick any super power?

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.982
- I think I'd want to be able to fly.

00:02:50.982 --> 00:02:51.815
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:51.815 --> 00:02:53.473
- Because I,
- Yes!

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.306
- I mean,
(audience applause)

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.140
saving the world is great,

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.260
but just to be able to look at everything

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.010
and just like transportation.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.312
- Yes!

00:03:02.312 --> 00:03:03.460
You're like, "I'll be there in a second."

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.460
(whooshing sound)

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.520
No traffic.
- And you can flex

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.507
on all your friends, like, "I can fly,

00:03:08.507 --> 00:03:11.787
"I'm taller than you."
(laughter)

